  "summary": {
    "plain": "KIMS searched its CsI(Tl) data for axions made in the Sun and found none, limiting how strongly such axions can couple to electrons.",
    "technical": "34,596 kg d of CsI(Tl) data; solar axions converting to electrons by the axio-electric effect; the limit is below the indirect solar-neutrino bound and fully excludes QCD axions heavier than 0.48 eV/c^2 (DFSZ) and 140.9 eV/c^2 (KSVZ)."
  },
